<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Protection Paladin Tank in Cataclysm Classic Pre-Raid. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Protection Paladin Tank Pre-Raid</h2>Pre-raid articles exist in a sort of limbo state whenever a new patch releases and not much will initially change. In the case of phase 2 &gt; 3, you'll see that a lot of gear retain a position in this guide as we feel that giving players a comprehensive perspective on the gearing process is important for pre-raid. Likewise we also want to curate the lists somewhat and cull unecessary items that we do not consider worthwhile. As such don't be alarmed if certain esoteric pieces do not make the list, especially if there are easy to obtain alternatives that we think you should focus on, such as PvP/<wbr/>Justice Points/<wbr/>Crafted (non raid mats), and reputation rewards. The latter especially is something we will always consider an "easy" to pick up piece unless that reputation is very grindy or an otherwise impediment.<br/>
<br/>Valor Points is a resource with a relatively limited acquisition rate, as the weekly amount you can gather is restricted. However the amount of "missed" valor points in any given week are added onto the next weeks permitted amount. What this means for players gearing for pre-raid is that later on in a given Cataclysm Classic phase, you'll be able, and expected to get more &amp; more VP gear to kit out your pre-raid sets.<br/>
<br/>To account for this, we have included two sets. The first one, which more accurately represents the "Early phase 3" pre-raid progression gear you might have if you did not raid previous phases. The second set which represents a "Late phase 3" potential gear setup wherein we have included a lot of optional crafted, BoE, and acquired a lot of the VP stuff.<ul>
<li class="fa fa-shield">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>
<i>Gearing to gear</i></b>
<br/>The phase 3 <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/news/elemental-rune-dungeons-and-protocol-inferno-available-for-testing-on-cataclysm-348666">catch-up gearing system</a> allows users to run existing heroic dungeons with additional mechanics, effects and difficulties. These dungeons open up an avenue for users to rapidly climb the ordinary gearing ladder or outright bypassing large sections of gearing. The caveat is that they will require you to have 346 item level to queue. While you could go there earlier with a fully premade group and manually enter, it's safe to say that most players will not do this.<br/>
<br/>This means that brand new players may have to <i>gear to gear</i>. To this end we want to highlight that you technically don't need to use the items in order to have its item level be counted to your stat card. You could technically have, as a <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_paladin.gif");'></span>
<span class="c2">Protection Paladin</span> a cloth belt, mail legs and so forth in your <b>inventory</b> inflating your item level for the purposes of queueing. We don't think you should outright steal items from players who could rightfully use them, though keep that in mind.<br/>
<br/>Likewise the fastest way to gear pre-raid is always going to be accessing the farm-able content ASAP and in phase 3 this is dungeons. Dungeons will almost always give you the fastest gearing curve even if you are not cutting any corners or jumping steps, going from Questing&gt;Dungeons&gt;Heroic Dungeons&gt;Inferno Protocol&gt;Raids is the norm for a reason. That said you should look at the auction house when you reach max level and see if you can pick up some cheap BoEs to help you skip the line a little bit.</div></li></ul>
