<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="rings-for-protection-paladin-tank-pre-raid">Rings for Protection Paladin Tank Pre-Raid</h4>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70940/deflecting-brimstone-band">
<img alt="Deflecting Brimstone Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_firelandsraid_03a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deflecting Brimstone Band</span></a> iIs probably pound for pound the best VP upgrade in this phase, if you're upgrading directly from a dungeon blue. The caveat being that you're potentially missing out on an earlier set bonush we can pretty easily make the recommendation in this case.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65372/permafrost-signet">
<img alt="Permafrost Signet" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_86.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Permafrost Signet</span></a> is purchased for 12 Fragments, though the price is misleading as you do not necessarily know what stats the ring will roll prior to buying and opening the bag. This may lead you to pay a fair bit more than what you initially expected, however otherwise this is a very strong ring.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60226/dargonaxs-signet">
<img alt="Dargonax's Signet" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubystar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dargonax's Signet</span></a> bought for a whopping 80 Fragments, is on the higher end of costs but is totally worth it. This ring is very heavy on mastery and if you're looking to fill out your stats it's an easy recommend.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71367/thecks-emberseal">
<img alt="Theck's Emberseal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_firelandsraid_02b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Theck's Emberseal</span></a> is technically not available pre-raid in that it drops exclusively from a raid zone. However being BoE you could theoretically purchase this and save yourself the trouble, while as it usually goes these are generally very expensive but we wanted to add this for posterity as prices may drop in the future. Or maybe you just have deep pockets.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70127/lylagar-horn-ring">
<img alt="Lylagar Horn Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_65.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lylagar Horn Ring</span></a> &amp; <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70126/nemesis-shell-band">
<img alt="Nemesis Shell Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_leather_shellfragment.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nemesis Shell Band</span></a> are available through a bit of a grind with the Molten Front and however it matches and exceeds everything else preceding it, certainly consider it at least. The latter however is mostly just catch up gear for players who can't or won't get the other options.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58187/ring-of-the-battle-anthem">
<img alt="Ring of the Battle Anthem" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_82.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of the Battle Anthem</span></a> is also made available in phase 3 from JP, easy recommendation in this case.<div class="box" data-level="null">
<b>Ring Enchants</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=74218/enchant-ring-greater-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Ring - Greater Stamina</span></a> -  Only Enchanters may apply Ring Enchants on their own rings.</div>
<div class="pad"></div>
